# treefrog-linux R36SX config fragment
#
# PURPOSE: apply on top of the SDK's kernel-squashfs.config (which is a generic
# base and is MISSING device-critical options that the stock R36SX kernel has).
#
# EVIDENCE (2026-09-09 physical boot test #1, docs/test-runs/2026-09-09_1934_r36sx.md):
#   - Our kernel booted the full stock stack (init, hcdaemon/AVP, icube, zhijack,
#     cubevol, picoarch, FrogUI menu rendered 4200+ frames; log.txt on SD).
#   - FrogUI menu did not respond to buttons: cubevol opens /dev/input/js0 (strings
#     of stock /mnt/g/rootfs/usr/bin/cubevol), picoarch reads /tmp/joy_key which
#     cubevol writes. Without /dev/input/js* (joydev), cubevol has no input source
#     -> FrogUI stuck with quit=0 -> console appears frozen at the TreeFrogUI logo.
#
# Rule: every line below must map to documented evidence (see docs/boards/r36sx.md
# and docs/research-log.md). Do not add options speculatively.

# --- input: joystick API for cubevol (/dev/input/jsN) -------------------------
CONFIG_INPUT_JOYDEV=y
